Remove dead vendored Apache BCEL (388 files, ~3 MB)

pluckyporcupine's migration vendored the full Apache BCEL 6.2 source tree
(ProjectFortress/src/org/apache/bcel/, 378 files) plus an unused bcel.jar
to satisfy a single import in MethodInstantiater.java:

    import com.sun.org.apache.bcel.internal.generic.INVOKEINTERFACE;

That import was dead code even in Sun's tree — the only INVOKEINTERFACE
the file uses is the ASM constant Opcodes.INVOKEINTERFACE. JDK 9's module
system turned the harmless dead import into a compile error; the correct
fix was deleting one line. Instead the import was repointed at a vendored
copy of BCEL, which javac has been compiling into every build since
(432 class files), referenced by nothing.

The ASM 9 rung (2f1fdbf2e) already removed the import itself. This
deletes the now fully unreferenced vendored tree, the dead jar, and the
two commented-out bcel classpath lines in build.xml.

Gate on JDK 25: ant testSystem 382/0/0, ant testFast zero failures,
both on a clean build without BCEL.

